  "id": "psychophysical-scaling",
  "term": "psychophysical scaling",
  "definition": "Psychophysical scaling is a method used to measure sensations and other conscious experiences quantitatively by relating them to stimulus intensity. The term also refers to the broader problem of creating scales that give consistent results across different investigators and laboratories.",
